+# Request: serve /v1/exports to StockGPT
+
+**From:** StockGPT (`prateek-sofo/stockgpt`). **Owner ruling (2026-11-19):** Sofo World is the one place that scrapes;
+StockGPT reads news, events, the competitor graph, financials and filings from it.
+
+## What this branch adds
+
+`backend/src/sofo_world/serve/exports.py`: four read-only routes under `/v1/exports` (`news`, `events`,
+`relationships`, `sec`), each a keyset page ordered by the time Sofo World recorded the row, with a `next` cursor.
+A consumer that stores the cursor receives every later row once. Any service key with the `read` scope may call
+them. Served: title, snippet and link of an article (7.7), public observations only (7.8), companies by ticker and
+CIK only. Test: `backend/tests/integration/test_exports_api.py`.
+
+## What it takes to turn it on
+
+1. Merge and deploy the API where it reads the live database (cc-1 on db-1: `infra/cc-aws/deploy.sh api`).
+2. Make `/v1/exports/` reachable for a machine with a key. Today the public site lets only signed-in browsers
+   through, to `/admin/` only:
+   - `infra/cc-aws/api.yaml`, nginx: add a `location /v1/exports/` that proxies to the API and keeps the
+     `Authorization` header (the `/admin/` block blanks it), and move the `x-sofo-email` check into the `/admin/`
+     block so it does not apply to this one. Keep the origin-secret check for both.
+   - `infra/cc-aws/edge/handler.mjs`: for a path that starts with `/v1/exports/`, skip the Cognito sign-in and pass
+     the request to the origin only when it carries `Authorization: Bearer sk_world_...`; otherwise answer 401. The
+     API still verifies the key against `service_keys`, so the edge check is only a first filter. Add the case to
+     `handler.test.mjs`.
+   - CloudFront already forwards the header (`AllViewerExceptHostHeader`).
+3. Mint a key: Command Center, Settings, API keys: consumer `stockgpt`, scope `read`. The answer shows
+   `SOFO_WORLD_URL` and `SOFO_WORLD_KEY` once.
+4. StockGPT side: `SOFO_WORLD_URL=... SOFO_WORLD_KEY=... python -m stockgpt.sources.sofo_api` (or `scripts/daily.sh`,
+   which calls it when both are set).
+
+An index on `news_articles (first_seen, article_id)` and on `observations (recorded_at, observation_id)` keeps the
+pages fast once the tables are large; `events (detected_at, sofo_event_id)` likewise. Not added here: a migration on
+the live tables is the owner's call.
+
+## Not verified here
+
+The route's SQL was run against a local Postgres 16 with the same column shapes, not against this repository's test
+database or the live one. `make test` and `make lint` have not been run on this branch.
